    "body": "There was no functional test covering the null output validation in `NormalizeOutputs()` at `rawtransaction_util.cpp:88`.\n\nThis adds an `assert_raises_rpc_error` check to the existing invalid outputs block in `rpc_rawtransaction.py`, verifying that passing a null output raises RPC error `-8` with the expected message: `Invalid parameter, output argument must be non-null`.\n\nThe test passes with the expected error message, and changing the expected message makes it fail, confirming that the assertion is actually being executed.\n\nValidated by running `rpc_rawtransaction.py` successfully.\n",
